<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andromeda Galaxy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Andromeda Galaxy is the nearest large spiral galaxy to the Milky Way, about 2.5 million light years away, and the most distant object easily visible to the naked eye. The Persian astronomer Abd al-Rahman al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> gave one of the earliest recorded descriptions of it, as a 'small cloud', in his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-fixed-stars">Book of Fixed Stars</a> of about 964. Its nature as a separate galaxy was established by Edwin Hubble in the 1920s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andromeda-galaxy.jpg" alt="Andromeda Galaxy" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lviatour · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M31-Andromede-16-09-2023-Hamois.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
